## maxogden/csv-spectrum — CSV parsing acid-test corpus

The conformance tests reproduce the full corpus published at
https://github.com/maxogden/csv-spectrum, pinned at commit
`d30e80f8b99d2eecb3778f1d7b9ed1cb425502ec` (tag `2.0.0`, 2024-07-04):

  * vendored verbatim under `src/testdata/csv-spectrum/` (12 `csvs/*.csv` +
    12 `json/*.json` fixture pairs, matched by basename per the corpus's own
    `index.js`)
  * driven mechanically by `src/csv_spectrum_vectors.zig` (one entry per
    pair, `@embedFile`d) and `src/csv_spectrum_test.zig` (the runner, which
    compares this module's parse of each `.csv` against its paired `.json` —
    never against this module's own prior output)

Excluded from vendoring, deliberately: the repository's own `.git/`,
`readme.md`, `index.js`, `test.js`, `package.json`/`package-lock.json`
metadata (none of it is test-fixture data).

The package declares its license as BSD-2-Clause in `package.json` (`"license":
"BSD-2-Clause"`); the repository carries no separate `LICENSE` file at the
pinned commit (confirmed via `git log --all -- LICENSE LICENSE.md
LICENSE.txt`, which returns nothing), so there is no license TEXT to reproduce
beyond that declaration and the author attribution below:

  csv-spectrum
  Copyright (c) max ogden
  https://github.com/maxogden/csv-spectrum
  License: BSD-2-Clause (as declared in package.json)

Only test-fixture text is reproduced. The implementation under test
(`LineIterator`/`splitFields` in `src/line.zig`) is the authors' own (MIT);
its DESIGN reference (RFC 4180) needs no entry per root `NOTICE` §0 (a public
spec is not itself a copyrightable work), and this codec's own README
"Provenance" note already says clean-room. Four of the corpus's 12 fixtures
are out of this module's documented scope (see `csv_spectrum_vectors.zig` for
the reason each is excluded) and are not asserted against, though they are
still counted and still driven through the parser to confirm it does not
crash on them.
